%U A378369 3,2,1,0,2,1,0,0,3,2,1,0,0,2,1,0,3,2,1
%N A378369 Distance between n and the least nonsquarefree number >= n.
%C A378369 All terms are 0, 1, 2, or 3 (cf. A078147).
%C A378369 From _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 05 2026: (Start)
%C A378369 The asymptotic densities of the occurrences of 0, 1, 2, and 3 are as follows:
%C A378369   0: 1 - 1/zeta(2) = 0.39207289814597337133... (A229099).
%C A378369   1: 1/zeta(2) - Product_{p prime} (1 - 2/p^2) = A059956 - A065474 = 0.28529300291478195808... .
%C A378369   2: Product_{p prime} (1 - 2/p^2) - Product_{p prime} (1 - 3/p^2) = A065474 - A206256 = 0.197147118033435372... .
%C A378369   3: Product_{p prime} (1 - 3/p^2) = A206256 = 0.125486980905809298334427999... . (End)
%H A378369 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A378369/b378369.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A378369 Asymptotic mean: Limit_{m->oo} (1/m) * Sum_{k=1..m} a(k) = Sum_{m=1..3} Product_{p prime} (1 - m/p^2) = A059956 + A065474 + A206256 = 1.056048181699080597577... . - _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 05 2026
%t A378369 Table[NestWhile[#+1&,n,SquareFreeQ[#]&]-n,{n,100}]
%o A378369 (PARI) a(n) = my(k = n); while(issquarefree(k), k++); k - n; \\ _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 05 2026
%Y A378369 Adding n to each term a(n) gives A120327.
